Importing `dynamo_timed` from the internal `torch._dynamo.utils` module is risky as internal APIs are subject to change or removal without notice in future PyTorch versions. While vLLM already uses this in other parts of the compilation stack, adding it to the distributed communication module increases the surface area of this dependency. It is recommended to wrap this import in a `try-except` block and provide a no-op fallback to ensure the engine remains functional if this internal utility is missing or moved in future Torch releases.

```suggestion
try:
    from torch._dynamo.utils import dynamo_timed
except ImportError:
    import contextlib
    def dynamo_timed(name): 
        if callable(name):
            return name
        return contextlib.nullcontext()
```

